WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.270
California, 2012 to 2016: one of
the most severe droughts on record.

2
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:12.590
In 2014, river water for farms in the
Central Valley was cut by about one-third.

3
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:18.410
Southern Ethiopia, from late 2020:
five rainy seasons in a row failed.

4
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:23.910
By April 2022, more than 8 million people
in southern and south-eastern Ethiopia

5
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.250
were affected.

6
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.070
Two long droughts.

7
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.050
So why were the results so different?

8
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.910
In this mission, you'll compare what
drought did to people and wildlife in each

9
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:34.850
place.

10
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.810
Then you'll find out who responded,
from households to governments,

11
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.050
and judge what made the difference.

12
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:46.290
Your mission: explain why drought hit
California and Ethiopia so differently.
